config ZENITH_DONGLE_BACKLIGHT_OFF_ON_USB_SUSPEND
    bool "Turn the Prospector backlight off while the USB host is suspended"
    default y
    depends on SHIELD_PROSPECTOR_ADAPTER && !PROSPECTOR_USE_AMBIENT_LIGHT_SENSOR
    help
      When the computer sleeps, the USB bus enters suspend. Drive the display
      backlight PWM to 0 then, and back to CONFIG_PROSPECTOR_FIXED_BRIGHTNESS on
      resume.

      This is deliberately NOT available with the ambient light sensor enabled.
      The module's ALS thread re-sets the backlight roughly every 100ms from its
      own light reading, so it would overwrite a 0 almost immediately and the
      screen would flicker rather than go dark. With the sensor disabled the
      module sets the brightness exactly once, at init, so a 0 written here
      stays put.

      ZMK's own display blanking is a different thing and does not replace this:
      it blanks the LCD controller only, leaving this separately-driven
      backlight lit.
